 split bean (the interior being white) is called white lentil. It should not be confused with the much smaller true black lentil (Lens culinaris)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-vigna-mungo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vigna_mungo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine",[["Dal makhani","dish/dal-makhani"],["Idli","dish/idli"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Urad dal","ingredient/urad-dal"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Urad (bean)","ingredient/urad-bean"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/6f/Black_gram.jpg/500px-Black_gram.jpg","w":500,"h":355,"by":"Sanjay Acharya","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_gram.jpg"}},"dish/khoresh-karafs":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/khoresh-karafs","n":"Khoresh karafs","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Iranian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Khoresh karafs is a traditional Iranian dish. As the name suggests, celery is the main part of this dish."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-khoresh-karafs"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khoresh_karafs"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Iranian cuisine","cuisine/iranian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Celery","ingredient/celery"],["Ver jus","ingredient/ver-jus"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Unicorns in the Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"unicornsinthekitchen.com","note":"Iranian-born Shadi HasanzadeNemati's blog with a large Persian recipe section.","url":"https://www.unicornsinthekitchen.com/persian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Iranian cuisine","links":[["Akuri","dish/akuri"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Chelow kabab","dish/chelow-kabab"],["Doogh","dish/doogh"],["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Juje